| **claim 3** (14.13: re-runs the inventory) | n/a, never reached the design | **DID NOT RE-RUN** — 3 lines in the map against 30 from its own named command |
| claim 1 (18.3: surfaces the scope decision) | **occasion destroyed by compliance** | — |
| tokens | 41,296 | 57,565 |

Opus on the identical conditions: **6/6 overrode**, **3/3 re-ran**.

**Two arms, two claims, both contradicting — and n=1 is not a rate.** The remaining four decide
whether this is the reversal 20.4 predicted or two draws from a middling coin, which is precisely
what 14.12 against 14.13 showed a single reading cannot tell apart.

One observation that is not a claim, recorded because it is cheap and may matter: q59 delivered
on **57,565 tokens** where the Opus arms on this condition spent 97,000–112,000. If that holds,
the tier comparison in 20.3 starts from a better place than the 2.54× overhead suggested.

